       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg per dose, four times daily, is 16 g/day. That is well into the toxic range, and I know of no indication where it would be appropriate. At that dose I'd expect a real risk of serious harm to the patient, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Normal baseline kidney and liver function wouldn't protect against that.\n\nI can do either of these right now:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 400 mg, 600 mg, or 800 mg PO at an appropriate frequency, staying at or under 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Consider alternatives.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than ibuprofen gives at its ceiling dose, I can enter a different agent or a multimodal regimen that you specify.\n\nIf you think this dose is truly needed, please talk with pharmacy or clinical toxicology first. I can enter the order after that, if it is clinically justified."
